{"case_id": "q016-batch", "row_id": "q016", "mode": "batch", "objective": "PLM-103 in vivo single-agent monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression tumour shrinkage in Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) animal models", "query": ["PLM-103 PDAC xenograft monotherapy tumour regression TGI"], "anchors": ["PLM-103"], "search_latency_ms": 454.9, "target": "PLM-103", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 384.7, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 7697, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000323, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 0, "abstain": true, "top_score": 0.0214, "results": [{"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "PLM-103 - Drug Targets, Indications, Patents - Patsnap Synapse", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/7b3e5bce8ca746e68b004c9c7068431f", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "Indication\nPhase\n...\nStudy\nPhase\nPopulation\nAnalyzed Enrollment\n...\nResults\nEvaluation\nPublication Date\nNo Data", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-11", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.92, "evidence": 0.0233}, "jev_score": 0.0214, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Evaluation of the safety, pharmacokinetics, and antitumor activity of ...", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S266636432500061X", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-06", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.54, "evidence": 0.0333}, "jev_score": 0.018, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Patient Derived Xenograft Models: An Emerging Platform for ...", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4167608/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "|(33)|PDAC|42|Primary|Surgery|Fresh tumor pieces in matrigel|Nude|s.c.|61 %|\n...\n|PDAC (26)|T/C < 20 %|Gemcitabine Erlotinib Temsirolimus|14|36 0 0|NA|\n|PDAC (33)|TGI > 85 %|Gemcitabine|23|17 %|Response to Gemcitabine in the PDX model predicted longer time to progression in patients.|\n...\nThese experiments show that the response rates in PDX models correlate with those observed in the clinic, both for targeted agents and for classic cytotoxics.\n...\nWith regards to conventional chemotherapy, studies in NSCLC, HBC, CRC and PDAC demonstrated that response rates to clinically used agents such as paclitaxel, carboplatin, gemcitabine, 5-fluorouracil, irinotecan and adriamycin, among others, are comparable between PDX models and clinical data (Table 3).\nMore recently, the role of PDX models as potential screening platforms for clinical trials has been also shown in a prospective study in PDAC.\nThis work showed that the combination of *nab*-paclitaxel and gemcitabine is effective in PDX models of PDAC, a finding that correlated with the clinical efficacy of this combination.\nIn fact, this regimen has recently been demonstrated to provide a survival benefit for patients with advanced PDAC in a randomized phase III study, and is likely to become a standard of care in this setting (38).", "date": "2014-07-15", "last_updated": "2026-08-21", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.03, "evidence": 0.24}, "jev_score": 0.0072, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "A potential therapeutic target for pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma", "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0022356525397867", "domain": "sciencedirect.com", "snippet": "You can set your browser to block or alert you about these cookies, but some parts of the site will not then work.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2025-09-03", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.2, "evidence": 0.0233}, "jev_score": 0.0047, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Biomimetic Tumour Model Systems for Pancreatic Ductal ...", "url": "https://research-portal.uu.nl/ws/files/268222329/ijms-26-06388.pdf", "domain": "research-portal.uu.nl", "snippet": "It has been reported that cell line-derived xenografts have predicted the therapeutic response in various cancers, including PDAC, inconsistently [123–125].\n...\nThe authors observed that there was a reduction in tumour volume with cetuximab compared to the untreated control group.\nMoreover, the reduction in tumour volume was more profound when treatment was combined with gemcitabine (~94.7% decrease in tumour cells for 32 ng/mL gemcitabine\nInt.\nJ. Mol.\nSci. 2025, 26, 6388\n15 of 54\nplus 2.5 µg/mL of cetuximab vs. a decrease of 10.5% in tumour cells without gemcitabine and only 2.5 µg/mL of cetuximab [126]).\nIn contrast, it was found in a phase III clinical trial that patients who had advanced pancreatic cancer treated with gemcitabine and a placebo or gemcitabine with cetuximab experienced no benefit from treatment [127].\nOther studies also further support the translational inconsistency between results seen with cell line-derived xenografts and clinical trials for various types of cancers [128,129].", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-13", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.02, "evidence": 0.16}, "jev_score": 0.0032, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "OpenLB Open Library of Bioscience", "url": "https://ngdc.cncb.ac.cn/openlb/publication/OLB-PM-37602328", "domain": "ngdc.cncb.ac.cn", "snippet": "- Wafik S El-Deiry: Laboratory of Translational Oncology and Experimental Cancer Therapeutics, Warren Alpert Medical School, Brown University, Providence, RI, United States.", "date": "2023-01-01", "last_updated": "2025-07-01", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.13, "evidence": 0.02}, "jev_score": 0.0026, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 1, "quer