": "NCT04194775Active, not recruitingPhase 3\n# A Multi-Center, Double-Blind, Randomized, Phase III Study to Investigate the Efficacy and Safety of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in Combination With Lenvatinib Compared to Placebo in Combination With Lenvatinib as First-Line Therapy in Subjects With Advanced Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC)\nCStone Pharmaceuticals125 sites in 6 countries534 enrolledStarted: December 13, 2019Last updated: July 30, 2026\n...\n- **Phase**\nPhase 3\n- **Status**\nActive, not recruiting\n...\n- **Enrollment**\n534\n...\n- **Primary Endpoint**\n...\nThis is a multi-center, double-blind, randomized, phase III study to investigate the efficacy and safety of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in combination with lenvatinib and placebo in combination with lenvatinib in the treatment of subjects with no prior systemic treatment and with unresectable advanced hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC).\n...\nResults posted to ClinicalTrials.gov on 2026-07-30.\n...\n534 started · 0 completed\n...\nJune 18, 2025 (last year)\n- **Study Completion**\nSeptember 30, 2026 (2 days ago)\n- **Last Verified**", "date": "2026-07-30", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.9733}, "jev_score": 0.9538, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Nofazinlimab - Drug Targets, Indications, Patents - Patsnap Synapse", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/bf31aad0266d41688ed754613150c716", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "|NCT04194775 (CS1003-305, ESMO2025)|Phase 3|Hepatocellular Carcinoma First line|534|Nofazinlimab + Lenvatinib|crgoxwqgbt(rzfiobiepn) = wfpwygxeca czvdkshulz (pvclpucluq ) View more|Positive|17 Oct 2025|\n|--|--|--|--|--|--|--|--|\n|NCT04194775 (CS1003-305, ESMO2025)|Phase 3|Hepatocellular Carcinoma First line|534|Placebo + Lenvatinib|crgoxwqgbt(rzfiobiepn) = cupywigtzp czvdkshulz (pvclpucluq ) View more|Positive|17 Oct 2025|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-08-15", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.96, "evidence": 0.8467}, "jev_score": 0.8128, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "A Study of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in Subjects With Advanced Hepatocellular Carcinoma", "url": "https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT04194775", "domain": "clinicaltrials.gov", "snippet": "Drug: Nofazinlimab (CS1003)+Lenvatinib Drug: Nofazinlimab (CS1003) Placebo+Lenvatinib\n- CS1003-305\n...\nInclusion criteria\n- Age ≥18 years on the day of signing informed consent-(For Taiwan, the lower limit of age is 20 years).\n- Subjects with unresectable advanced HCC, that is not eligible for surgery and/or locoregional therapy (Stage B or C based on Barcelona Clinic Liver Cancer [BCLC] staging system, and meets either one of the following criteria: 1) histologically or cytologically confirmed diagnosis of HCC, 2) clinically confirmed diagnosis of HCC according to American Association for the Study of Liver Diseases (AASLD) criteria.\nPatients without cirrhosis require histological confirmation of diagnosis.\n- With at least one measurable lesion can be assessed\n- Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group performance status (ECOG PS) 0 or 1.\n- Life expectancy ≥ 3 months.\n- Child-Pugh A\n- No prior systemic treatment for advanced HCC\n- Subjects with hepatitis B virus (HBV) infection, are willing to continue receiving antiviral treatment while on study.\nSubjects have adequate organ and marrow function.\nFemale subjects with childbearing potential must have negative serum pregnancy test result at screening.\nFemale subjects with childbearing potential, and male subjects and their female partners with childbearing potential must agree to use an contraceptive method(s) from the day of signing informed consent form (ICF), during the study and till at least 6 months after the last dose of study treatment.\nExclusion criteria\n- Fibrolamellar-HCC, sarcomatoid, cholangiocellular carcinoma or mixed cholangiocarcinoma and HCC.\n- A prior bleeding event due to esophageal within 6 months or other gastrointestinal bleeding events within 28 days prior to screening.\n- Malabsorption syndrome or inability to take oral medication due to other causes.\n- HBV and HCV co-infection.\n- Investigator evaluates to increase the drug related risk caused by enrolling subjects in trial and taking study drug, or any serious or uncontrolled systematic disease that confound the drug absorption or the study outcome, e,g diabetes mellitus, hypertension, rheumatoid arthritis, major cardiovascular disease and so on.\n- Surgery or locoregional therapy for palliative purpose within 4 weeks prior to study treatment.\n- History of other malignancy(ies) in the past 5 years, except for malignant disease treated with curative intent and without active disease.\n- Known history of human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection or acquired immunodeficiency syndrome (AIDS).\n- Current or prior use of systemic corticosteroid (> 10 mg/day prednisone or equivalent) or other immunosuppressive medication within 14 days prior to the first dose of study treatment.\n- History of bone marrow transplantation or organ transplantation.\n- History of anaphylaxis or hypersensitivity to any ingredient of the investigational product.\n- Any contraindication of lenvatinib.\n- Known history of drugs abuse that would interfere with cooperation with the requirements of the trial.\n- Pregnant or lactating female subjects.\n- History of psychiatric disease that would interfere with cooperation with the requirements of the trial; lack of or with restricted physical capability.\n- QTc interval > 470 msec (as calculated with Fridericia's formula) at screening electrocardiogram (ECG);\n- Any condition that would in the investigator's judgment, prevent the subject from participating in this study.\n...\n|Overall survival (OS)|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|\n...\n|Objective response rate (ORR) assessed by blinded independent central review committee(BICR)|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|\n|Progression-free survival(PFS) assessed by blinded independent central review committee(BICR) based on Response Evaluation Criteria in Solid Tumors(RECIST) v1.1|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|\n...\n|Percentage of Participants with Adverse Events|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|\n|Peak and trough serum concentrations of CS1003|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|\n|Number and percentage of subjects who develop anti-CS1003 antibody (ADA)|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|\n|Time to deterioration (TTD), defined as the time from randomization to the first deterioration of European Organization for the Research and Treatment of Cancer (EORTC) Quality-of-Life Questionnaire Core 30 (QLQ-C30) scale|Expected to be 5.5 years after the first patient is enrollment.|", "date": "2019-12-10", "last_updated": "2025-08-12", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.7833}, "jev_score": 0.7598, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Liver Epithelial Neoplasm", "url": "https://www.cancerindex.io/cancer/liver-epithelial-neoplasm/trials?status=ACTIVE_NOT_RECRUITING", "domain": "cancerindex.io", "snippet": "|NCT04770896|A Study of Atezolizumab With Lenvatinib or Sorafenib Versus Lenvatinib or Sorafenib Alone in Hepatocellular Carcinoma Previously Treated With Atezolizumab and Bevacizumab(IMbrave251)|active not recruiting|Phase 3|557|Hoffmann-La RocheINDUSTRY|28|Aug 25, 2026|clinicaltrials|\n...\n|NCT06618300|Streamlined Resin Y90 Radiation Segmentectomy for Small HCC(One&Done)|active not recruiting|—|30|UNC Lineberger Comprehensive Cancer CenterOTHER|1|Aug 13, 2026|clinicaltrials|\n...\n|NCT04194775|A Study of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in Subjects With Advanced Hepatocellular Carcinoma|active not recruiting|Phase 3|534|CStone PharmaceuticalsINDUSTRY|6|Jul 30, 2026|clinicaltrials|\n...\n|NCT04523493|Phase III Study of Toripalimab（JS001） Combined With Lenvatinib for Advanced HCC|active not recruiting|Phase 3|530|Shanghai Junshi Bioscience Co., Ltd.OTHER|5|Jul 6, 2026|clinicaltrials|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-19", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.85, "evidence": 0.7867}, "jev_score": 0.6687, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Current status of the cost burden of first-line systemic treatment for ...", "url": "https://academic.oup.com/jjco/article/54/10/1071/7687758", "domain": "academic.oup.com", "snippet": "Thus, there is currently no consensus on the use of atezolizumab plus bevacizumab, durvalumab and tremelimumab for the treatment of advanced HCC.\nAdditionally, many ongoing trials still use TKIs as controls since trials comparing TKIs and ICIs were initiated almost simultaneously, and several trials have not yet reported their results (Table 2).\n...\n| |NCT04194775|Nofazinlimab (anti-PD-1 antibody) plus lenvatinib|Lenvatinib|III|OS|First-line|\n...\n| |NCT03764293|SHR-1210 (anti-PD-1 antibody) plus apatinib (TKI)|Sorafenib|III|OS & PFS|First-line|", "date": "2024-10-03", "last_updated": "2026-08-27", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.94, "evidence": 0.7033}, "jev_score": 0.6611, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "A Study of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in Subjects With Advanced Hepatocellular Carcinoma", "url": "https://www.cancerindex.io/trial/NCT04194775", "domain": "cancerindex.io", "snippet": "NCT04194775CI-TRIAL-00119920active not recruitingPhase 3Results postedClinicalTrials.gov clinicaltrialsProvenance- **Source**\n...\n### Dates and enrollment\n- **Start**\nDec 13, 2019\n- **Primary completion**\nJun 18, 2025\n- **Completion**\nSep 30, 2026\n- **First posted**\nDec 11, 2019\n- **Last update posted**\nJul 30, 2026\n- **Results first posted**\nJul 30, 2026\n- **Enrollment**\n534 (actual)", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-19", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.74, "evidence": 0.8433}, "jev_score": 0.624, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "A Study to Evaluate MIV-818 in Patients With Liver Cancer Manifestations", "url": "https://med.agiltrace.com/clinical-trials/NCT03781934", "domain": "med.agiltrace.com", "snippet": "No results posted yet for this study\n...\nThis is an open-label, multicentre dose escalation/expansion study to assess safety and tolerability of MIV 818 as either monotherapy or in combination with 1) lenvatinib, a tyrosine kinase inhibitor used as a standard of care for the treatment of HCC or 2) pembrolizumab, a PD-1 inhibitor.\n...\n## Timeline & Regulatory\n- **Start**\n2018-09-05\n- **Primary Completion**\n2025-01-07\n- **Completion**\n2025-06-16\n...\n- A Study of Nofazinlimab (CS1003) in Subjects With Advanced Hepatocellular Carcinoma\nNCT04194775 ·Status: ACTIVE_NOT_RECRUITING ·Phase: PHASE3\n- Lenvatinib in Patients With Previously Treated Advanced Biliary Tract Cancer\n...\n- HAIC Plus Lenvatinib and Toripalimab for Advanced HCC", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-05", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.82, "evidence": 0.7533}, "jev_score": 0.6177, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Lenvatinib for the Treatment of Recurrent Hepatocellular Carcinoma After Liver Transplant", "url": "https://med.agiltrace.com/clinical-trials/NCT05103904", "domain": "med.agiltrace.com", "snippet": "No results posted yet for this study\n...\nThis phase II trial evaluates lenvatinib for the treatment of hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC) that has come back (recurrent) after a liver transplant.\n...\n## Eligibility\n- **Min Age**\n18 Years\n- **Sex**\nALL\n- **Healthy Volunteers**\nNo\n## Timeline & Regulatory\n- **Start**\n20