{"case_id": "q031-batch", "row_id": "q031", "mode": "batch", "objective": "SPR2015 in vivo single-agent monotherapy tumour growth inhibition TGI tumour regression or shrinkage in Pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC) animal models", "query": ["SPR2015 HPAC xenograft TGI percentage monotherapy", "SPR2015 AsPC-1 xenograft tumour regression shrinkage", "SPR2015 PDAC monotherapy xenograft tumour growth inhibition", "SPR2015 HPAC AsPC-1 xenograft AACR 2026 abstract 5978"], "anchors": ["SPR2015"], "search_latency_ms": 747.0, "target": "SPR2015", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 413.3, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 7974, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000335, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 9, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.7631, "results": [{"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "KRAS G12D Inhibitor's $2.13B Deal Tests Cross-Border Tech Transfer", "url": "https://www.pharmtech.com/view/kras-g12d-inhibitor-s-2-13b-deal-tests-cross-border-tech-transfer", "domain": "pharmtech.com", "snippet": "- SPR2015 functions as an ON-state molecular glue, showing nanomolar antiproliferative activity in KRAS G12D cell lines with wild-type selectivity and tumor regression in xenograft models.\n...\nSPR2015 is described as a molecular glue inhibitor that engages the ON form of the mutant protein.^1^ It showed nanomolar antiproliferative activity across multiple KRAS G12D-mutant cell lines while maintaining selectivity over wild-type cells, and it demonstrated monotherapy antitumor efficacy in cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft models.", "date": "2026-09-28", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.7867}, "jev_score": 0.7631, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "MSD takes a $400m bite of SciBrunch's KRAS drug", "url": "https://pharmaphorum.com/news/msd-takes-400m-bite-scibrunchs-kras-drug", "domain": "pharmaphorum.com", "snippet": "The company reported studies at this year's American Association for Cancer Research (AACR) congress which showed antitumour efficacy for SPR2015 as a monotherapy across multiple *in vivo* cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft models.", "date": "2026-10-02", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7267}, "jev_score": 0.7122, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck Enters into Exclusive Global License Agreement ...", "url": "https://www.merck.com/news/merck-enters-into-exclusive-global-license-agreement-with-scibrunch-therapeutics-for-spr2015-an-investigational-oral-kras-g12d-on-inhibitor/", "domain": "merck.com", "snippet": "In addition, SPR2015 has demonstrated compelling antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple in vivo cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft (CDX/PDX) models, as reported in preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting.", "date": "2026-10-02", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7133}, "jev_score": 0.699, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck licenses SPR2015, an oral KRAS G12D inhibitor, from ...", "url": "https://chemxplore.com/news/merck-scibrunch-spr2015-kras-g12d-license", "domain": "chemxplore.com", "snippet": "- SPR2015 is a preclinical oral KRAS G12D (ON) molecular‑glue inhibitor showing nanomolar antiproliferative activity and monotherapy efficacy in CDX and PDX models.\n...\nSPR2015 is an investigational preclinical oral KRAS G12D (ON) molecular‑glue inhibitor that has demonstrated nanomolar antiproliferative activity in various KRAS G12D‑mutant cell lines with good selectivity over KRAS wild‑type cells.\nIt has shown antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple in vivo cell‑derived and patient‑derived xenograft (CDX/PDX) models, with preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting.", "date": "2026-09-28", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7067}, "jev_score": 0.6926, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck Licenses Preclinical KRAS G12D Inhibitor from SciBrunch", "url": "https://www.pharmexec.com/view/merck-licenses-preclinical-kras-g12d-inhibitor-scibrunch", "domain": "pharmexec.com", "snippet": "KRAS G12D is the most common oncogenic RAS mutation found in human tumors, arising from a substitution of glycine with aspartate at position 12, a change that leaves KRAS active and continuously signaling for cell proliferation and survival.^1^ SPR2015 has also shown compelling antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple in vivo cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft models, according to preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR Annual Meeting.^2^", "date": "2026-09-28", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7033}, "jev_score": 0.6892, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Revolution Medicines - MedPath Trial", "url": "https://trial.medpath.com/organization/revolution-medicines", "domain": "trial.medpath.com", "snippet": "- SPR2015 is a molecular glue inhibitor that showed nanomolar antiproliferative activity in KRAS G12D-mutant cell lines with selectivity over KRAS wild-type cells, plus monotherapy antitumor activity in xenograft models.", "date": "2026-09-28", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.68}, "jev_score": 0.6664, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "SPR2015: Merck Pays $400M, Up to $2.13B - novapharmanews.com", "url": "https://novapharmanews.com/apac/news/spr2015-merck-400m-2-13b-license", "domain": "novapharmanews.com", "snippet": "- SPR2015 is still preclinical.\nThe release cites nanomolar cell-line activity and tumor activity in xenograft models shown at AACR 2026, without a response rate.\n...\nIt also cites antitumor activity as a single agent in cell-derived and patient-derived xenografts, from preclinical data presented at the 2026 AACR meeting.\nNo tumor-shrinkage percentage is printed.", "date": "2026-09-29", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.6733}, "jev_score": 0.6531, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck, SciBrunch Launch Up-to-$2.13B Collaboration ...", "url": "https://www.genengnews.com/topics/cancer/merck-scibrunch-launch-up-to-2-13b-collaboration-to-develop-preclinical-kras-inhibiting-molecular-glue/", "domain": "genengnews.com", "snippet": "At the 2026 American Association for Cancer Research (AACR) Annual Meeting, a team of SciBrunch researchers that included founder, chairman, and CEO Tao Hu, PhD, presented preclinical data showing SPR2015 to have demonstrated what it termed compelling antitumor efficacy as a monotherapy across multiple *in vivo* cell-derived and patient-derived xenograft (CDX and PDX) models.\n...\nIn a head-to-head mouse study comparing a single oral once-daily dose at 100 mg/kg of SPR2015 to another unspecified G12D (ON) inhibitor in over 15 CRC CDX or PDX models, SPR2015 showed significantly superior efficacy in the *in vivo* CRC xenograft models, achieving a 64.7% objective response rate (ORR) and 94.1% disease control rate (DCR) as monotherapy.", "date": "2026-09-29", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.96, "evidence": 0.6633}, "jev_score": 0.6368, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Anirban Maitra on X: \"This #AACR26 abstract is worth $400 ...", "url": "https://x.com/Aiims1742/status/2104884186620494308", "domain": "x.com", "snippet": "Abstract 5978: SPR2015, a highly potent and selective KRAS G12D (on) inhibitor, exhibits favorable...", "date": "2026-09-29", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.96, "evidence": 0.54}, "jev_score": 0.5184, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "Merck–SciBrunch SPR2015 Deal | Lucid Diligence Brief - LucidQuest", "url": "https://www.lqventures.com/merck-scibrunch-spr2015-deal-diligence-brief/amp/", "domain": "lqventures.com", "snippet": "SciBrunch’s AACR 2026 abstract described it as IND-enabling and projected Phase 1 entry by the end of 2026.\n(AACR abstract 5978, Reuters)", "date": "2026-09-29", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.92, "evidence": 0.47}, "jev_score": 0.4324, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": false, "reason": "low_evidence"}], "total_ms": 1160.3, "ts": "2026-10-06T12:18:11+00:00"}
