{"case_id": "q045-batch", "row_id": "q045", "mode": "batch", "objective": "BMF-500 first regulatory approval or market launch year in acute myeloid leukemia", "query": ["BMF-500 first regulatory approval AML", "BMF-500 expected regulatory approval AML", "BMF-500 market launch AML", "BMF-500 expected launch date AML"], "anchors": ["BMF-500"], "search_latency_ms": 726.1, "target": "BMF-500", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 505.3, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 9176, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000385, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 10, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.8672, "results": [{"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Biomea Fusion (BMEA) FDA Approvals, PDUFA Dates & Drug Alerts 2026 $BMEA", "url": "https://www.marketbeat.com/stocks/NASDAQ/BMEA/fda-events/?drug=icovamenib&anchor=fda-icovamenib-2026-06-05", "domain": "marketbeat.com", "snippet": "Given that the GLP-1 receptors in monkeys are functionally similar to those in humans, the findings support further clinical development of BMF-650 as a promising, patient-friendly treatment for obesity.Read Announcement BMF-500 FDA Regulatory Timeline and Events BMF-500 is a drug developed by Biomea Fusion for the following indication: Orally Bioavailable Covalent Inhibitor of FLT3.\nThis drug is under review by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA).\nBelow is a timeline of key regulatory milestones for this therapy.\nUpdated data - June 13,2025Updated Data Phase 1Drug: BMF-500Announced Date: June 13, 2025Indication: Orally Bioavailable Covalent Inhibitor of FLT3 AnnouncementBiomea Fusion, Inc.\nannounced updated preliminary clinical data from the ongoing Phase I COVALENT-103 trial of BMF-500 in adults with relapsed or refractory (\"R/R\") acute leukemia (\"AL\").\n...\nThe trial focuses on safety, pharmacokinetics, and early signs of clinical activity in heavily pretreated patients, many with FLT3 mutations.\nSignificant data include bone marrow blast reductions in several patients, with some achieving a complete remission with incomplete hematologic recovery or a morphologic leukemia-free state.\n...\nThe study has enrolled 20 patients with relapsed or refractory acute leukemia, including 13 with FLT3 mutations, all of whom had previously failed treatment with gilteritinib.\n...\nIn the past two years, Biomea Fusion (BMEA) has not received FDA approval for any therapies.\nHowever, the company does have drugs under review or in active clinical development.\n...\nIn the past two years, Biomea Fusion (BMEA) has reported FDA regulatory activity for the following drugs: icovamenib, BMF-650, BMF-500, BMF-219 and COVALENT-111.", "date": "2026-06-08", "last_updated": "2026-06-22", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.96, "evidence": 0.9033}, "jev_score": 0.8672, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "BMF-500 - Drug Targets, Indications, Patents", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/0e8fac2d50284b9fac3c91177d16d79c", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "|Active Indication Acute Myeloid Leukemia|\n...\n|Drug Highest PhasePhase 1|\n|First Approval Date-|\n...\n|--|--|--|--|--|\n|Acute Myeloid Leukemia|Phase 1|United States|Biomea Fusion, Inc.|26 Jul 2023|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-24", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.8833}, "jev_score": 0.8568, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "EX-99.1", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1840439/000095017024039304/bmea-ex99_1.htm", "domain": "sec.gov", "snippet": "In 2023, reported initial topline data from Phase 1 study of BMF-219 in acute myeloid leukemia (AML); continuing to progress COVALENT-101 in liquid tumors, COVALENT-102 in solid tumors and COVALENT-103 (BMF-500) in AML.\n...\nIn 2023 BMF-500 entered the clinic as the only covalent FLT3 inhibitor in clinical development.”\n...\nWe expect these data will inform potentially registrational studies, which we plan to start in 2025, pending discussions with regulatory authorities.\n...\n•\nAnnounced FDA clearance of IND for BMF-500 in COVALENT-103, a Phase 1 study, and started enrollment of Biomea’s novel third generation investigational oral covalent inhibitor of FMS-like tyrosine kinase 3 (FLT3).", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-29", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.8567}, "jev_score": 0.8396, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "10-K - SEC.gov", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1840439/000119312526121825/bmea-20251231.htm", "domain": "sec.gov", "snippet": "We have a limited operating history, limited experience in conducting clinical trials, have not completed the clinical development of any product candidates, have no products approved for commercial sale, and have not generated any revenue, which may make it difficult for you to evaluate our current business and likelihood of success and viability.\n...\nIn September 2025, we announced that we received IND clearance from the FDA for BMF-650, and initiated our ongoing Phase I trial in obese, otherwise healthy volunteers.\nIn January 2025, we announced that we plan to conclude our studies exploring icovamenib’s potential in oncology and explore partnerships to further advance our oncology assets, including BMF-500.\n...\nWe have not received marketing approval for any product candidate, and we have not generated any revenue from any product sales or other sources since our inception.\nWe do not expect to generate revenue unless or until we successfully complete preclinical and clinical development and obtain regulatory approval of, and then successfully commercialize, at least one product candidate.\n...\nIn September 2025, we announced that BMF-650, our investigational, next-generation, oral small molecule GLP-1 RA, received IND-clearance from the FDA.\nInitiation of our Phase I GLP-131 trial for BMF-650 in obese, otherwise healthy volunteers is ongoing, and data is anticipated in the second quarter of 2026.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-25", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.91, "evidence": 0.9133}, "jev_score": 0.8311, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Biomea Fusion, Inc.", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/organization/26bae87fc714320a3f21ce8509ae5e58", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "|Inactive Indication Acute Myeloid Leukemia [+12]|\n|Drug Highest PhasePhase 2|\n|First Approval Ctry.\n/ Loc.-|\n|First Approval Date-|\nBMF-500\n|Target FLT3|\n...\n|Active Indication Acute Myeloid Leukemia|\n|Inactive Indication-|\n|Drug Highest PhasePhase 1|\n|First Approval Ctry.\n/ Loc.-|\n|First Approval Date-|\n...\n|BMF-500 ( FLT3 )|Acute Myeloid Leukemia More|Phase 1|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.96, "evidence": 0.8233}, "jev_score": 0.7904, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Biomea Fusion Announces FDA Clearance of Investigational New Drug (IND) Application for Covalent FLT3 Inhibitor BMF-500 in Relapsed or Refractory Acute Leukemia | Biomea Fusion", "url": "https://investors.biomeafusion.com/news-releases/news-release-details/biomea-fusion-announces-fda-clearance-investigational-new-drug-1/", "domain": "investors.biomeafusion.com", "snippet": "Biomea Fusion Announces FDA Clearance of Investigational New Drug (IND) Application for Covalent FLT3 Inhibitor BMF-500 in Relapsed or Refractory Acute Leukemia\n- BMF-500, a novel 3rd generation covalent inhibitor of fms-like tyrosine kinase 3 (FLT3), is the second investigational compound, discovered and developed by Biomea’s FUSION™ System, to advance to the clinic.\n- Phase I study (COVALENT-103) of BMF-500 will examine its safety and efficacy in patients with relapsed or refractory acute leukemia with FLT3 wild-type and FLT3 mutations, including those with MLLr / NPM1 mutations.\n...\nREDWOOD CITY, Calif., May 01, 2023 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- Biomea Fusion, Inc.\n(“Biomea” or “the company”) (Nasdaq: BMEA), a clinical-stage biopharmaceutical company dedicated to discovering and developing novel covalent small molecules to treat and improve the lives of patients with genetically defined cancers and metabolic diseases, today announced that the U.S.\nFood and Drug Administration (FDA) has cleared the company's Investigational New Drug (IND) application to begin a Phase I trial (COVALENT-103) of BMF-500, an investigational covalent FLT3 inhibitor, in adult patients with relapsed or refractory acute leukemia.\n...\nAny forward-looking statements in this press release are based on our current expectations, estimates and projections only as of the date of this release and are subject to a number of risks and uncertainties that could cause actual results to differ materially and adversely from those set forth in or implied by such forward-looking statements, including the risk that we may encounter delays in preclinical or clinical development, the preparation, filing and clearance of INDs, patient enrollment and in the initiation, conduct and completion of our ongoing and planned clinical trials and other research and development activities.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2024-02-04", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.7767}, "jev_score": 0.7534, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Loading Inline Form.", "url": "https://www.sec.gov/ix?doc=/Archives/edgar/data/0001840439/000095017024118366/bmea-20240930.htm", "domain": "sec.gov", "snippet": "In January 2022, we announced that we had initiated dosing in COVALENT-101, a Phase 1 clinical trial to explore the safety and efficacy of icovamenib in patients with relapsed/refractory AML and acute lymphoblastic leukemia (ALL), including those with MLL/KMT2A gene arrangements or NPM1 mutations.\n...\nIn December 2023, we reported the achievement of minimal residual disease negativity (MRD-neg) in first complete responder in a participant with AML.\n...\nIn May 2022, we announced the nomination of our second development candidate, BMF-500, a third-generation oral covalent small molecule inhibitor of activating mutations of the FMS-like tyrosine kinase 3 (FLT3), which are the most frequent genetic alt\neration in AML and are associated with poor prognosis.\n...\nIn May 2023, we announced FDA clearance of our IND to study BMF-500 in a Phase 1 study (COVALENT-103) examining safety and efficacy in patients with relapsed or refractory acute leukemia with FLT3 wild-type and FLT3 mutations, including those with MLLr/NPM1 mutations.\nIn \nOctober 2023, we announced the first participant had been dosed with BMF-500 in relapsed or refractory acute leukemia.\nWe anticipate that the dose escalation for COVALENT-103 will be completed by year end 2024.\n...\nIn addition, our lead product candidate, icovamenib, is in clinical development, and we dosed the first participant with our second product candidate, BMF-500, in October 2023, following clearance of our IND by the FDA in May 2023.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-21", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.94, "evidence": 0.7933}, "jev_score": 0.7457, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "A Phase 1, Study of BMF-500 in Adults With Acute Leukemia - Clinical Trial for Acute Myeloid Leukemia | NCT05918692 | Trials.co", "url": "https://trials.co/clinical-trials-details/-/NCT05918692", "domain": "trials.co", "snippet": "Study Start Date\nJuly 26, 2023 (Actual)\nPrimary Completion Date\nJuly 31, 2025 (Anticipated)\nStudy Completion Date\nJuly 31, 2026 (Anticipated)\n...\nA Phase 1 first-in-human dose-escalation and dose-expansion study of BMF-500, an oral FLT3 inhibitor, in adult patients with acute leukemia.\n...\nA Phase 1 first-in-human dose-escalation and dose-expansion study of BMF-500, an oral covalent FLT3 inhibitor, in adult patients with acute myeloid leukemia (AML), acute lymphocytic leukemia (ALL) and Acute Mixed-Phenotype Leukemia (MPAL) who may or may not be on Antifungals.", "date": "2023-04-10", "last_updated": "2026-09-11", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.7033}, "jev_score": 0.6822, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Biomea Fusion Reports Second Quarter 2025 Financial ...", "url": "https://investors.biomeafusion.com/news-releases/news-release-details/biomea-fusion-reports-second-quarter-2025-financial-results-and", "domain": "investors.biomeafusion.com", "snippet": "**BMF-500 (Oral Small Molecule FLT3 Inhibitor in Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML))**\n- Presented updated Phase I data at EHA 2025, showing sustained antileukemic responses, deep bone marrow blast reductions, and survival benefit in relapsed/refractory FLT3-mutant AML patients, all of whom had failed FLT3 inhibitor gilteritinib.\n- The Company concluded its oncology efforts and is now exploring strategic partnerships for BMF-500.", "date": "2025-08-05", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.6867}, "jev_score": 0.6661, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "BMF-500 / Biomea Fusion - LARVOL DELTA", "url": "https://delta.larvol.com/Products/?ProductId=7dcd09a2-09b0-4543-b9f1-8d95262deb65", "domain": "delta.larvol.com", "snippet": "## COVALENT-103: A Phase 1 Study of BMF-500 in Adults With Acute Leukemia (clinicaltrials.gov) - P1 | N=35 | Completed | Sponsor: Biomea Fusion Inc. | Active, not recruiting ➔ Completed | Trial primary completion date: Apr 2026 ➔ Jan 2026\n...\n## COVALENT-103: A Phase 1 Study of BMF-500 in Adults With Acute Leukemia (clinicaltrials.gov) - P1 | N=35 | Active, not recruiting | Sponsor: Biomea Fusion Inc. | Recruiting ➔ Active, not recruiting | N=84 ➔ 35 | Trial primary completion date: Jul 2025 ➔ Jan 2026", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-24", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.96, "evidence": 0.6167}, "jev_score": 0.592, "jev_rank": 10, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}], "total_ms": 1231.4, "ts": "2026-10-06T12:18:14+00:00"}
{"case_id": "q047-batch", "row_id": "q047", "mode": "batch", "objective": "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor first regulatory approval or market launch year for acute myeloid leukemia", "query": ["Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor Insilico Medicine AML approval launch", "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor Insilico Medicine AML regulatory timeline", "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor AML first market launch year"], "anchors": ["Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor", "CDK12"], "search_latency_ms": 573.3, "target": "Dual CDK12/13 Inhibitor / CDK12", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 422.8, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 7650, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000321, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 9, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.5934, "results": [{"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "JMC｜With generative AI assistance, Insilico Medicine ...", "url": "https://www.eurekalert.org/news-releases/1074881", "domain": "eurekalert.org", "snippet": "Insilico Medicine (\"Insilico\"), a clinical stage generative artificial intelligence (AI)-driven biotechnology company, today announced the publication of a novel series of orally available covalent CDK12/13 dual inhibitors, as a potential option against refractory and treatment-resistant cancers.\nPublished in the ***Journal of Medicinal Chemistry* ** (IF=7.2), the study showcases the discovery of compound 12b, a potent, selective, and safe therapy targeting CDK12/13, empowered by Insilico’s proprietary generative AI platforms including PandaOmics and Chemistry42.\n...\nDuring the preclinical *in vitro* and *in vivo* testing, compound 12b demonstrated nanomolar potencies across cancer cell lines, desirable ADME properties.\nFurthermore, 12b exhibited significant efficacy in breast cancer and acute myeloid leukemia (AML) models, all without inducing intolerable side effects, paving the way for further therapeutic development.\n...\n\"The research and development process showcases how AI-guided drug design can achieve both precision and safety in cancer therapeutics, and we are striving to advance the compound in this program into clinical trials in the near future.\"", "date": "2025-02-26", "last_updated": "2026-04-21", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.86, "evidence": 0.69}, "jev_score": 0.5934, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "CDK12/13 TARGET therapy (InSilico Medicine) - Patsnap Synapse", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/drug/d4f56c4afbbf4e43805fc7050386be8a", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "CDK12/13 TARGET therapy (InSilico Medicine)\n...\nTarget\nCDK12 x CDK13\nAction\ninhibitors\nMechanism\nCDK12 inhibitors(cyclin dependent kinase 12 inhibitors),\nCDK13 inhibitors(cyclin dependent kinase 13 inhibitors)\nTherapeutic Areas\nNeoplasms\nActive Indication\nSolid tumor\n...\nOriginator Organization\nInSilico Medicine Hong Kong Ltd.\n...\nDrug Highest Phase\nPreclinical\nFirst Approval Date\n...\nChina\nInSilico Medicine Hong Kong Ltd.\n11 Jun 2024", "date": "2025-05-08", "last_updated": "2026-02-07", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.85, "evidence": 0.6933}, "jev_score": 0.5893, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "CDK12/13", "url": "https://insilico.com/pipeline_target_cdk12/13", "domain": "insilico.com", "snippet": "Cyclin-dependent kinase 12/13 (CDK12/13) Inhibitor:\nTreating Tumors through Induction of BRCAness\n(IND-Enabling)\nAssays Completed\nWholly-owned and Available for Licensing\n- *In vivo* efficacy studies – Combo study with Olaparib and Cisplatin\n- *In vivo* efficacy studies – Single agent\n- *In vivo* PK-PD\n- *In vivo* PK studies\n- *In vitro* ADMET studies\n- Developability/CMC\n- *In vitro* cell-based\n- Toxicology studies\n- Enzymatic\n...\nInsilico Medicine CDK12 Inhibitor Summary – IND-Enabling\n...\nEffective in both mono and combo therapies\n...\n- Potential broader indications such as AML, HCC, SCLC, Colorectal cancer, and Ovarian c