{"case_id": "q059-batch", "row_id": "q059", "mode": "batch", "objective": "HEC234055 in vivo animal models and results: cell-line xenograft (CDX), patient-derived xenograft (PDX), syngeneic, orthotopic, genetically engineered models", "query": ["HEC234055 HNSCC xenograft", "HEC234055 PDX model", "HEC234055 syngeneic model", "HEC234055 orthotopic pancreatic model", "HEC234055 genetically engineered mouse model"], "anchors": ["HEC234055"], "search_latency_ms": 499.8, "target": "HEC234055", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 367.5, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 7929, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000333, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 2, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.7404, "results": [{"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "C262019A_Sunshine Pharma 1..4", "url": "https://www.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0423/2026042301900_c.pdf", "domain": "hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "二、HEC234055 — 攻克「不可成藥」靶點的口服高活性Pan-RAS分子膠抑制劑（摘\n要號#2634）\n...\n亞型仍存在巨大未滿足的臨床需求。在研產品HEC234055 為本集團自主研發\n的口服高活性Pan-RAS 分子膠抑制劑，旨在廣譜覆蓋KRAS 多種突變及野生型\n擴增。此次公佈的臨床前數據亮點如下：\n...\n廣譜覆蓋與高活性：可同時作用於KRAS 的活性（三磷酸鳥苷（「GTP 」）結\n合）與非活性（GDP 結合）狀態，並覆蓋G12D 、G12C 、G12V 、G13D 、\nQ61H等多種突變類型及野生型擴增。\n...\n亞納摩爾級細胞活性：在多種KRAS 突變驅動的癌細胞系中，其抗增殖活\n性達到亞納摩爾級別，半抑制濃度（「IC50」）低至0.49 納摩爾（「n M」），顯\n示出優於當前對標分子的強效抑制能力。\n...\n顯著的體內療效：在多種KRAS 突變的異種移植瘤模型中（涵蓋胰腺癌、\n肺癌及結直腸癌），口服給藥可產生劑量依賴性的腫瘤生長抑制乃至誘導\n腫瘤消退。", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-06-01", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.7633}, "jev_score": 0.7404, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] E262019A_Sunshine Pharma 1..4 - HKEXnews", "url": "https://www1.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0423/2026042301899.pdf", "domain": "www1.hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "HEC234055 — Orally Available High-Activity Pan-RAS Molecular Glue Inhibitor\nTargeting the ‘‘Undruggable’’ (Abstract #2634)\nRAS gene mutations drive approximately one-quarter of human cancers, with common mutation subtypes such as KRAS G12D and G12V still representing significant unmet clinical needs.\nThe drug candidate under development HEC234055 is an orally available high-activity Pan-RAS molecular glue inhibitor independently developed by the Group, designed to target a broad spectrum of multiple KRAS mutations as well as wild-type amplifications.\n...\nBroad-spectrum coverage and high activity: It can act on both active (guanosine triphosphate (‘‘GTP’’)-bound) and inactive (GDP-bound) states of KRAS, and covers various mutation types such as G12D, G12C, G12V, G13D, Q61H, and wild-type amplification.\n...\nSignificant in vivo efficacy: In multiple KRAS-mutated xenograft tumor models\n(including pancreatic, lung and colorectal cancers), oral administration can produce\ndose-dependent tumor growth inhibition and even induce tumor regression.\n...\nExcellent in vivo efficacy: In MC38-hPDL1 homology models and multiple PBMC humanized xenograft models, the tumor growth inhibition rate (TGI) of single- agent administration can reach up to approximately 70%. In particular, in PD-L1 antibody-insensitive models such as NCI-H358 (non-small cell lung cancer) and\nMDA-MB-231\n(triple-negative\nbreast\ncancer),\nthe\nsingle-agent\nefficacy\nof\nHEC201625 is significantly superior to that of PD-L1 antibodies, demonstrating a differentiated advantage.\n...\nThe preclinical research data disclosed in this announcement are derived from laboratory and animal model studies, and the relevant drug candidates have not yet undergone clinical trials\nin\nhumans.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-04-23", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.94, "evidence": 0.76}, "jev_score": 0.7144, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Resource Page", "url": "https://www.wagnerlab.net/resource-page", "domain": "wagnerlab.net", "snippet": "This page lists genetically engineered mouse models generated and published by our team and how to obtain them from public repositories (links to repositories not shown on the mobile page).", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-01", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.13, "evidence": 0.1967}, "jev_score": 0.0256, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "PDX Models - PDXNet", "url": "https://www.pdxnetwork.org/models", "domain": "pdxnetwork.org", "snippet": "Models available for research are listed in CancerModels.org.\n...\nPDXNet researchers generated 520 new PDX models across 56 cancer types.\nThe PDXNet Portal can be referenced for an up-to-date list of PDXNet-generated models.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-30", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.06, "evidence": 0.18}, "jev_score": 0.0108, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "PDX Model Database Registration", "url": "https://www.crownbio.com/databases/pdx-models", "domain": "crownbio.com", "snippet": "Our online, searchable patient-derived xenograft (PDX) database enables scientists around the world to quickly and easily search for models that meet their specific research needs.\n...\n**Browse the collection to:**\n- Access a diverse collection of over 2,400 well-characterized and ready-for-service PDX models from US, European, and Asian populations\n- Evaluate and filter models based on indication, target, growth characteristics, standard of care treatment, and ethnicity", "date": "2025-09-26", "last_updated": "2026-07-28", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {"on_target": 0.09, "evidence": 0.11}, "jev_score": 0.0099, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "MMRRC Repository", "url": "https://www.mmrrc.org/", "domain": "mmrrc.org", "snippet": "STOCK Tg(Cxcr4-EGFP)CD73Gsat/Mmucd is available from the MMRRC and contains multiple copies of a modified BAC in which EGFP reporter gene is inserted immediately upstream of the coding sequence of the targeted gene.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.05, "evidence": 0.1033}, "jev_score": 0.0052, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "Find Your Research Mouse Model 丨 ...", "url": "https://en.gempharmatech.com/product/searchByNcbi_18783_1.html", "domain": "en.gempharmatech.com", "snippet": "Use this search tool to find knockout, knock-in, transgenic, humanized mouse models and more by gene, disease area, or model type.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-07-24", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.06, "evidence": 0.02}, "jev_score": 0.0012, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "International Mouse Strain Resource", "url": "https://www.findmice.org/", "domain": "findmice.org", "snippet": "The IMSR is a searchable online database of mouse strains, stocks, and mutant ES cell lines available worldwide, including inbred, mutant, and genetically engineered strains.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.03, "evidence": 0.03}, "jev_score": 0.0009, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Find Your Research Mouse Model 丨 GemPharmatech", "url": "https://en.gempharmatech.com/product/search_608.html", "domain": "en.gempharmatech.com", "snippet": "Use this search tool to find knockout, knock-in, transgenic, humanized mouse models and more by gene, disease area, or model type.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-05-19", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.05, "evidence": 0.0067}, "jev_score": 0.0003, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "{{ngMeta['og:title']}}", "url": "https://bio.tools/pdxnet_portal", "domain": "bio.tools", "snippet": "This is a development version of the re