{"case_id": "q058-batch", "row_id": "q058", "mode": "batch", "objective": "HEC234055 in vivo efficacy in combination with another agent in Pancreatic Ductal Adenocarcinoma, including the combination partner", "query": ["HEC234055 combination pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma in vivo", "HEC234055 combination partner PDAC xenograft", "HEC234055 AACR 2026 combination efficacy"], "anchors": ["HEC234055"], "search_latency_ms": 523.2, "target": "HEC234055", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 921.7, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8066, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000339, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 2, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.771, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "C262019A_Sunshine Pharma 1..4", "url": "https://www.hkexnews.hk/listedco/listconews/sehk/2026/0423/2026042301900_c.pdf", "domain": "hkexnews.hk", "snippet": "本集團欣然宣佈，於2026 年4 月17 日至22 日在美國加利福尼亞州聖地亞哥舉行的\n...\n二、HEC234055 — 攻克「不可成藥」靶點的口服高活性Pan-RAS分子膠抑制劑（摘\n要號#2634）\n...\n的口服高活性Pan-RAS 分子膠抑制劑，旨在廣譜覆蓋KRAS 多種突變及野生型\n...\n亞納摩爾級細胞活性：在多種KRAS 突變驅動的癌細胞系中，其抗增殖活\n性達到亞納摩爾級別，半抑制濃度（「IC50」）低至0.49 納摩爾（「n M」），顯\n示出優於當前對標分子的強效抑制能力。\n...\n顯著的體內療效：在多種KRAS 突變的異種移植瘤模型中（涵蓋胰腺癌、\n肺癌及結直腸癌），口服給藥可產生劑量依賴性的腫瘤生長抑制乃至誘導\n腫瘤消退。\n...\n廣泛的聯合用藥潛力：與化療藥物(5 -FU) 、抗VEGF 抗體、VEGFR 抑制劑\n及KRAS G12C抑制劑聯合給藥，均表現出顯著的協同增效作用。", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-06-01", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.7867}, "jev_score": 0.771, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "Sunshine Lake Pharma Co., Ltd. Showcases Three Innovative ...", "url": "https://www.marketscreener.com/news/sunshine-lake-pharma-co-ltd-showcases-three-innovative-oncology-drug-candidates-at-2026-aacr-annu-ce7f58d8dd8ffe27", "domain": "marketscreener.com", "snippet": "At the 2026 Annual Meeting of the American Association for Cancer Research (AACR), held from 17 to 22 April 2026 in San Diego, California, USA, the Group presented the latest preclinical research results of three oncology pipeline candidates through three poster presentations.\n...\nHEC234055 is an orally available high-activity Pan-RAS molecular glue inhibitor independently developed by the Group, designed to target a broad spectrum of multiple KRAS mutations as well as wild-type amplifications.\n...\nSignificant in vivo efficacy: In multiple KRAS-mutated xenograft tumor models (including pancreatic, lung and colorectal cancers), oral administration can produce dose-dependent tumor growth inhibition and even induce tumor regression.\n...\nThe preclinical research data disclosed in this announcement are derived from laboratory and animal model studies, and the relevant drug candidates have not yet undergone clinical trials in humans.", "date": "2026-04-23", "last_updated": "2026-05-14", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.96, "evidence": 0.6633}, "jev_score": 0.6368, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Unbiased in vivo preclinical evaluation of anticancer drugs identifies effective therapy for the treatment of pancreatic adenocarcinoma - PubMed", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/33199632/", "domain": "pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "To identify effective PDAC therapies, we leveraged a syngeneic orthotopic PDAC transplant mouse model to perform a large-scale, in vivo screen of 16 single-agent and 41 two-drug targeted therapy combinations in mice.\nAmong 57 drug conditions screened, combined inhibition of heat shock protein (Hsp)-90 and MEK was found to produce robust suppression of tumor growth, leading to an 80% increase in the survival of PDAC-bearing mice with no significant toxicity.\nMechanistically, we observed that single-agent MEK inhibition led to compensatory activation of resistance pathways, including components of the PI3K/AKT/mTOR signaling axis, which was overcome with the addition of HSP90 inhibition.\nThe combination of HSP90(i) + MEK(i) was also active in vitro in established human PDAC cell lines and in vivo in patient-derived organoid PDAC transplant models.\nThese findings encourage the clinical development of HSP90(i) + MEK(i) combination therapy and highlight the power of clinically relevant in vivo model systems for identifying cancer therapies.", "date": "2020-12-01", "last_updated": "2025-07-20", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.34, "evidence": 0.5}, "jev_score": 0.17, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "Closing Plenary Session examined highlights from the ...", "url": "https://www.aacrmeetingnews.org/closing-plenary-session-examined-highlights-from-the-aacr-annual-meeting-2026/", "domain": "aacrmeetingnews.org", "snippet": "Daraxonrasib, a multi-RAS-ON inhibitor recently reported to be effective against pretreated, metastatic pancreatic cancers, was found to also be effective in the first-line setting, either as monotherapy or in combination with chemotherapy.", "date": "2026-04-30", "last_updated": "2026-09-22", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.15, "evidence": 0.2267}, "jev_score": 0.034, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "[PDF] AACR DRUG DISCOVERY AND DEVELOPMENT (AACR D3)", "url": "https://www.aacr.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/D32026_AbstractTitlesOnly.pdf", "domain": "aacr.org", "snippet": "B068 A sphingolipid-derived paclitaxel nanovesicle enhances efficacy of combination therapies in triple-negative breast cancer and pancreatic cancer.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-07-13", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.09, "evidence": 0.18}, "jev_score": 0.0162, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "Advances in antibody-drug conjugates in cancer - PMC - NIH", "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13332605/", "domain": "pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov", "snippet": "Across multiple preclinical and early clinical studies, emerging ADC technologies demonstrated improved precision, enhanced efficacy, and the ability to overcome resistance mechanisms that have historically limited this class of therapeutics.", "date": "2026-07-04", "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.05, "evidence": 0.3033}, "jev_score": 0.0152, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "AACR Annual Meeting 2026 – Post-event summary", "url": "https://www.insights.bio/bioinsights/journal/article/3821/aacr-annual-meeting-2026-postevent-summary-clinical-data-readouts-and-emerging-themes", "domain": "insights.bio", "snippet": "TNG961 caused complete tumor regression in pancreatic and lung cancer models and demonstrated combinatorial activity with inhibitors targeting MTAP deletion, which frequently co-occurs.", "date": "2026-05-14", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.06, "evidence": 0.1333}, "jev_score": 0.008, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "AACR 2026: Emerging Antibody-Drug Conjugates for the ...", "url": "https://www.adcreview.com/conference-coverage/aacr/aacr-2026-emerging-antibody-drug-conjugates-for-the-treatment-of-solid-tumors-part-1/", "domain": "adcreview.com", "snippet": "IN30758, a novel ADC being developed by InxMed (Ying Shi Bio), targets integrins such as *alphaVbeta6*, an epithelial-specific transmembrane receptor that is typically absent in healthy adult tissues but significantly upregulated during wound healing, chronic inflammation, and in various solid epithelial cancers, including pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma (PDAC), non-small cell lung cancer (NSCLC), and ovarian cancer.", "date": "2026-05-05", "last_updated": "2026-10-03", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.03, "evidence": 0.0767}, "jev_score": 0.0023, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}