{"case_id": "q060-batch", "row_id": "q060", "mode": "batch", "objective": "EOM613 sponsor development stage indication public source", "query": ["EOM613 Crohn's disease trial current status", "EOM613 Crohn's disease Phase 2 initiation 2026", "EOM613 Crohn's disease clinical trial registry"], "anchors": ["EOM613 Crohn's disease", "EOM613"], "search_latency_ms": 440.0, "target": "EOM613 Crohn's disease / EOM613", "ok": true, "error": null, "jev_latency_ms": 905.8, "calls": 10, "attempts": 10, "usage": {"input_tokens": 8633, "output_tokens": 360}, "cost_usd": 0.000363, "n_candidates": 10, "n_kept": 7, "abstain": false, "top_score": 0.9604, "results": [{"rank": 1, "query_index": null, "title": "EOM Pharmaceutical Holdings Reports Promising Preclinical", "url": "https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/01/07/3214524/0/en/eom-pharmaceutical-holdings-reports-promising-preclinical-results-and-provides-an-update-on-eom613-and-eom147.html", "domain": "globenewswire.com", "snippet": "In 2025, the company completed IND-enabling toxicological and dosing preclinical animal studies for EOM613 with favorable results.\n...\nBased on these data, combined with previously reported promising results of our Phase I/IIa 2023 human clinical trial in hospitalized COVID-19 patients with cytokine-driven respiratory inflammation in Brazil, we are planning an initial Phase II exploratory clinical trial in patients with Crohn’s disease.\nThis trial is designed to include 15-20 patients and will be conducted at clinical sites in New Brunswick and Lakewood, NJ, under Principal Investigator Arkady Broder, MD, Director of Gastroenterology at the St. Peter’s Healthcare System.\nThe trial will enroll subjects with moderate to severe Crohn’s disease who have failed or could not tolerate at least one conventional therapy.\nEOM anticipates initiating the trial in the first quarter 2026 to test for signs of clinical remission and endoscopic remission with EOM613 treatment and to measure biomarkers such as C-reactive protein, calprotectin and pro-inflammatory serum cytokines.\n...\nIn light of the Brazilian clinical trial results, the company is currently preparing to initiate an EOM613 clinical program in Crohn’s disease.", "date": "2026-01-07", "last_updated": "2026-05-19", "orig_rank": 1, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.98}, "jev_score": 0.9604, "jev_rank": 1, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 2, "query_index": null, "title": "EOM Pharmaceutical Holdings Reports FDA Clearance of ...", "url": "https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/05/27/3301943/0/en/eom-pharmaceutical-holdings-reports-fda-clearance-of-an-ind-for-a-clinical-trial-in-cachectic-cancer-patients.html", "domain": "globenewswire.com", "snippet": "The trial is anticipated to be initiated early in the third quarter of 2026.\nThe Company is also planning an additional exploratory, open-label EOM613 clinical trial in Crohn’s disease.\nThis trial is intended to be conducted at clinical sites in New Brunswick and Lakewood, NJ, under Principal Investigator Arkady Broder, MD, Director of Gastroenterology at the St. Peter’s Healthcare System.\nThe trial is planned to enroll 15 to 20 subjects with moderate to severe Crohn’s disease who have failed or could not tolerate at least one conventional therapy.\nEOM anticipates initiating the trial in the fourth quarter 2026 to test for signs of both clinical remission and endoscopic remission with EOM613 monotherapy treatment and to measure biomarkers such as C-reactive protein, calprotectin and pro-inflammatory serum cytokines.", "date": "2026-05-27", "last_updated": "2026-05-28", "orig_rank": 2, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.9467}, "jev_score": 0.9183, "jev_rank": 2, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 6, "query_index": null, "title": "EOM Pharmaceutical Holdings Provides an Update on its Lead Drug Candidate EOM613", "url": "https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/eom-pharmaceutical-holdings-provides-an-update-on-its-lead-drug-candidate-eom613-301978052.html", "domain": "prnewswire.com", "snippet": "In light of these clinical trial results, the company is currently preparing to initiate an EOM613 clinical program in Crohn's disease.\n...\n\"EOM is now planning and designing a future clinical program for Crohn's disease patients who have failed currently available therapies or are unable to tolerate them,\" stated Shalom Z. Hirschman, MD, Chief Medical Officer of EOM.\n...\nEOM is planning to undertake IND-enabling animal toxicology and preclinical studies relevant to Crohn's disease.\nEOM is also assembling a team of key opinion leader gastroenterologists, who are experts in clinical research relating to novel treatment approaches to IBD, to advise on the design and execution of the planned clinical trial.\n...\n\"EOM's priority is to initiate a clinical program in inflammatory bowel disease as soon as possible,\" added Irach B. Taraporewala, PhD, Chief Executive Officer of EOM.", "date": "2023-11-07", "last_updated": "2025-07-05", "orig_rank": 6, "answers": {"on_target": 0.98, "evidence": 0.8833}, "jev_score": 0.8656, "jev_rank": 3, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 3, "query_index": null, "title": "ImmunoCellular Therapeutics Ltd. - Drug pipelines, Patents, Clinical ...", "url": "https://synapse.patsnap.com/organization/5ce8654ab76cb12db589696a5cb380f9", "domain": "synapse.patsnap.com", "snippet": "Clinical Trials associated with ImmunoCellular Therapeutics Ltd.\nNCT05212532\n/ Unknown statusPhase 1\nA Proof-of-Concept Study Evaluating Safety, Tolerability, and Preliminary Efficacy of EOM613 in COVID-19 Infected Patients With Severe Symptoms\n...\nIn light of these clinical trial results, the company is currently preparing to initiate an EOM613 clinical program in Crohn's disease.\n...\n\"EOM is now planning and designing a future clinical program for Crohn's disease patients who have failed currently available therapies or are unable to tolerate them,\" stated Shalom Z. Hirschman, MD, Chief Medical Officer of EOM.\n...\nEOM is planning to undertake IND-enabling animal toxicology and preclinical studies relevant to Crohn's disease.\n...\nThis exploratory Phase 1/2a clinical trial (NCT05212532), designated RESCUE, was a proof-of-concept, open-label study evaluating the safety, tolerability, and preliminary efficacy measures, such as the effects on serum cytokines, when EOM613 was added to the standard-of-care therapy.\n...\nEOM613, administered by subcutaneous (SC) injection was well-tolerated by hospitalized COVID-19 patients.\n...\n|AVR-118|Crohn Disease More|Preclinical|", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-09-30", "orig_rank": 3, "answers": {"on_target": 0.97, "evidence": 0.8567}, "jev_score": 0.831, "jev_rank": 4, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 10, "query_index": null, "title": "FDA Clears IND for EOM613 Trial in Cancer Cachexia Patients", "url": "https://www.clinicaltrialvanguard.com/news/fda-clears-ind-for-eom613-trial-in-cancer-cachexia-patients/", "domain": "clinicaltrialvanguard.com", "snippet": "Cancer cachexia has killed patients before their underlying malignancy could, yet across decades of failed trials no drug has earned FDA approval for the condition — and EOM Pharmaceutical Holdings is now cleared to run only a 20-patient open-label Phase 2a study to test whether that changes.\n...\nThe company’s simultaneous planning for a Crohn’s diseaseCrohn’s disease trial in Q4 2026 signals an intent to validate EOM613’s cytokine-modulation mechanism across indications rather than commit resources to a single confirmatory cachexia program.\nThe real test of whether this IND clearance matters will be the proportion of enrolled patients who achieve re-eligibility for chemotherapy by month three — that single number, more than any weight or appetite metric, determines whether a Phase 2b with a harder endpoint is fundable.", "date": "2026-05-30", "last_updated": "2026-09-24", "orig_rank": 10, "answers": {"on_target": 0.95, "evidence": 0.85}, "jev_score": 0.8075, "jev_rank": 5, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 9, "query_index": null, "title": "Methods of treating inflammatory bowel diseases", "url": "https://patents.google.com/patent/WO2025049974A1/en", "domain": "patents.google.com", "snippet": "In some aspects, a therapeutically effective amount of EOM613 is 2mls twice daily for a sufficient period of time to achieve a therapeutic benefit (e.g., at least 2 weeks, for example, 2 to 4 weeks or 2 to 8 weeks).\n- a therapeutically effective amount encompasses a fractional dose that contributes in combination with previous or subsequent a\n...\n- This nucleopeptide conjugate has a MW 2215 peptide moiety attached to a 740 MW nonpeptidic adduct to give a total MW of 2955.", "date": "2024-08-30", "last_updated": "2025-07-20", "orig_rank": 9, "answers": {"on_target": 0.92, "evidence": 0.5}, "jev_score": 0.46, "jev_rank": 6, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 8, "query_index": null, "title": "EOM Pharmaceutical Holdings Reports FDA Clearance of ...", "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/sectors/healthcare/articles/eom-pharmaceutical-holdings-reports-fda-123000259.html", "domain": "finance.yahoo.com", "snippet": "# EOM Pharmaceutical Holdings Reports FDA Clearance of an IND for a Clinical Trial in Cachectic Cancer Patients\n...\nMONTVALE, N.J., May 27, 2026 (GLOBE NEWSWIRE) -- **EOM Pharmaceutical Holdings, Inc.\n**(OTC: IMUC) (\"EOM\", the \"Company\") an innovative clinical-stage biotechnology company focused on developing transformative treatments for chronic inflammatory conditions and retinal diseases, is pleased to announce that the FDA has cleared its Investigational New Drug (IND) application to conduct a three-month Phase 2a clinical study of EOM613 in cachectic cancer patients.\n...\nEOM filed an IND application for the treatment of cachectic cancer patients at the FDA's Office of Cardiology, Hematology, Endocrinology and Nephrology Diseases (OCHEND) to conduct an open-label Phase 2 trial with Stage 4 cancer patients.\n...\nThe open-label clinical trial is designed to explore the effect of daily subcutaneous administration of EOM613 over a period of three months on weight, lean body mass, appetite, performance status and standardized measures of patient quality of life.\nIn addition, the safety and tolerability of EOM613 will be assessed.\n...\nAbout 20 patients, aged 18-80, are expected to be enrolled into the study.\nPatients at baseline will have a Karnofsky Performance Score of 40-80% and a life expectancy of at least four months.\nThe trial is anticipated to be initiated early in the third quarter of 2026.\n...\nThe Company is also planning an additional exploratory, open-label EOM613 clinical trial in Crohn's disease.\nThis trial is intended to be conducted at clinical sites in New Brunswick and Lakewood, NJ, under Principal Investigator Arkady Broder, MD, Director of Gastroenterology at the St.\nPeter's Healthcare System.\nThe trial is planned to enroll 15 to 20 subjects with moderate to severe Crohn's disease who have failed or could not tolerate at least one conventional therapy.\nEOM anticipates initiating the trial in the fourth quarter 2026 to test for signs of both clinical remission and endoscopic remission with EOM613 monotherapy treatment and to measure biomarkers such as C-reactive protein, calprotectin and pro-inflammatory serum cytokines.", "date": "2026-05-27", "last_updated": "2026-09-26", "orig_rank": 8, "answers": {"on_target": 0.72, "evidence": 0.6333}, "jev_score": 0.456, "jev_rank": 7, "kept": true, "reason": "kept"}, {"rank": 4, "query_index": null, "title": "Clinical Trials in the European Union - EMA", "url": "https://euclinicaltrials.eu/", "domain": "euclinicaltrials.eu", "snippet": "This website provides information on individual clinical trials in the European Union and European Economic Area since its launch on 31 January 2022.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-03-10", "orig_rank": 4, "answers": {"on_target": 0.07, "evidence": 0.01}, "jev_score": 0.0007, "jev_rank": 8, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 7, "query_index": null, "title": "Find Studies | ClinicalTrials.gov", "url": "https://clinicaltrials.gov/find-studies", "domain": "clinicaltrials.gov", "snippet": "A patient registry is a type of observational study.\n**Note:** The ClinicalTrials.gov results database became available in September 2008.\nOlder studies are unlikely to have results available in the database.\nThe results submitted date indicates when the study sponsor or investigator first submitted summary results information or submitted changes to summary results information.\n...\nIf there is a date listed for results submitted to ClinicalTrials.gov, but there is not a subsequent date listed for results returned after quality control review, this means that the submission is pending review by NLM.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-03-18", "orig_rank": 7, "answers": {"on_target": 0.03, "evidence": 0.0067}, "jev_score": 0.0002, "jev_rank": 9, "kept": false, "reason": "low_on_target"}, {"rank": 5, "query_index": null, "title": "ICTRP Search Portal - World Health Organization (WHO)", "url": "https://www.who.int/tools/clinical-trials-registry-platform/the-ictrp-search-portal", "domain": "who.int", "snippet": "The ICTRP Search Portal aims to provide a single point of access to information about ongoing and completed clinical trials.\nIt provides a searchable database containing the trial registration data sets made available by data providers around the world meeting criteria for content and quality control.\nTrial registration data sets are available on the ICTRP Search Portal in English only.\nSome data providers, however, may also store trial registration data sets in other languages.\nIf available, these may be searched by going directly to the web sites\nof the individual registries.", "date": null, "last_updated": "2026-10-02", "orig_rank": 5, "answers": {